    "Na__Asset__Description"  :  "Bespoke Vale cupola gutter (the cupola's cornice and gutter, which the hipped glazed lantern's kerb seats on): a 50 band 16.2 proud, a 14 fillet 37.25 proud, an ovolo R30 into a straight and a cove R32.25 out to a 15 lip 90.44 proud; 119 high, flat top. Traced from the Vale CAD for 64589 Abbasi (24-Nov-2026): the Front (both cupola ends) and Left elevations draw it end-on and agree to 0.05 mm; the built test sweep matched within 0.1 mm every 2 mm. Datum 0,0 = the cupola wall face at the underside (CAD 5011.27: place at 5011 so the top lands on 5130), outward -y. Saved on the MANAGER's ruling for Adam's review.",
